  "notes": "Warm off-white editor for a student radio-story assignment (Spanish class). Each source type has a color identity carried consistently across bin left-bars, transcript speaker names and timeline clips: teal narration, mustard sounds, indigo Don Arturo, rose Abuela Rosa. Teacher feedback is the pedagogical layer: numbered amber dots appear on the timeline ruler and inline in the transcript, matching numbered cards in the right panel with timecode chips, category tags (Pronunciation, Structure), Done checkboxes, a computed 'still in your story' status note and a one-click fix action (Re-record this line). A length meter against a 4:00 target turns red past the limit, and the ruler shades the over-time zone with a red dashed line and hatched stripe. A 'Past tenses' switch colors past-tense verbs, a teaching aid tied to the grammar goal. Keyboard shortcuts are shown as mono keycaps. Hidden tabs (verified live): Story order is a reorderable list of cards with drag handles and up/down arrows; Rubric shows 75/100 with per-criterion progress bars and checkmarks."
}
